@@ -2,6 +2,26 @@
 
 These files connect the Apple SEP kernel driver to the shared APFS xART
 gigalocker and the desktop fingerprint stack.
+
+`aurora-sep-export-attestation --output-dir /tmp/sep-attestation` exports
+committed-UIK attestation of the driver's existing machine ref-key and
+the corresponding public point. It needs the matching
+`SEP_BIO_EXPORT_ATTESTATION` ioctl, CAP_SYS_ADMIN, and permission to open
+`/dev/sep-bio`.
+The output directory must be new; it is created with mode 0700 and its files
+with mode 0600. The command never exports a private key, requests certificate
+issuance, creates a missing ref-key, or replaces an existing output. A persisted
+reference may be loaded read-only when the driver's cache is empty. The DER
+may be an encrypted envelope: it is preserved verbatim after removing SEP
+transport framing. `ENOKEY` means the existing key is unavailable; `ENOTTY`
+means the running module predates this interface. Building a new module does
+not activate the ioctl; do not reload an attached SEP to try it.
+Add `--include-system-public-keys` to also retrieve SIK `(1,1)` and committed
+UIK `(2,2)` via `SEP_BIO_SYSTEM_PUBLIC_KEY`, saving `SIKPub.bin` and `UIKPub.bin`.
+These outputs are opaque `oskgp` public data; the exporter makes no assumption
+about their encoding and preserves their bytes. The getter requires the standard
+SKS success-status/blob framing and fails on an unexpected response. Its live
+framing must still be verified when this driver build is activated.
 
 The current release installer and matched packages are published in
 [omacom/linux-aurora](https://github.com/omacom/linux-aurora/releases/latest):
